SUMMARY:Wizarding School at Linden Hall
DESCRIPTION:During Wizarding School\, campers are sorted into one of four Houses named after the first four Heads of School at Linden Hall. Participants have time to bond with their housemates and compete together to earn House points. They also take classes such as Potion Making\, Nature Studies\, Transformative Spells\, and Spells & Incantations. Additionally\, campers try out clubs\, such as Wand Dueling and Wizards Chess. \nDay: July 13-17 \nOvernight: July 12-17 \nTake a look at many more Summer Camps offered throughout Lancaster County this summer!\n\nAdditional Fun Things for Kids To Do in Lancaster?\n\n\nSummer Camps\nPetting Zoo\nRailroad Attractions\n\n\n\nFun on the Farm\nAmusement Parks\nMini Golf\n\n\n\nArcades & Video Games\nZip-Lines\nEvents Calendar
